<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Höxter</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Höxter is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weser">Weser</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. It grew up beside the abbey of Corvey, founded nearby in 822, whose abbots claimed lordship over it, and it was a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a>. Corvey's Carolingian westwork is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hoxter.jpg" alt="Höxter" width="320" height="270" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Spunky · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rathaus_H%C3%B6xter.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
